    "details": "VulnCheck reports:\n\n> Ten vulnerabilities fixed in SQLite 3.54.0 were published on\n> 2026-10-30. Four of them corrupt the heap: buffer overflows in the\n> FTS5 functions fts5MergeRowidLists() and fts5DoSecureDelete() and in\n> the session extension sessionUpdateFind(), and a use-after-free in the\n> R-Tree function nodeWrite(). A fifth, a use-after-free in the FTS3\n> function fts3BestSnippet(), is reached through snippet().\n>\n> The remaining five crash the process or leak data: unbounded recursion\n> through a chain of common table expressions, through a chain of\n> COLLATE operators and through countOfViewOptimization() in a VALUES\n> clause, an information leak on a page size mismatch in the write-ahead\n> log, and an authorizer bypass with RIGHT or FULL JOIN USING.\n>\n> An attacker has to supply a database file or SQL text, so the FTS5 and\n> FTS3 issues apply wherever those options are built in; both are on by\n> default in databases/sqlite3.\n",
    "id": "FreeBSD-2026-0573",
